# Friends — security baseline

Priority: **SECURITY > confidentiality > authorization > integrity > availability > convenience**.

Workflow: skill [friends-security](../skills/friends-security/SKILL.md). Hub: [docs/security/](../../docs/security/README.md).

## MUST

- Server-side **authn + authz** (room membership / host). JWT ≠ right to another room’s votes.
- Validate all external input; minimize response DTO / Prisma `select`.
- HIGH/CRITICAL fix → regression in the same PR when possible.
- Stop + user confirmation before: prod DB, secret rotation, destructive migration, auth architecture change.

## MUST NOT

- Assume “we have a guard/DTO/rate limit → safe”.
- Log or return: JWT, Discord access/refresh tokens, OAuth `code`, `Authorization`.
- Trust the Activity client or Discord payload without server verification.
- Ask for **values** of secrets (names only).
- Attack production or invent security theater.

## Scope

`apps/api`, `apps/activity`, `packages/db`, `packages/types`.
